  "note": "Split engine, no numeric score. validateB1(state) is a completeness validator: it walks b1Rules in array order, counts every rule whose applies(state) is true into totalRequired, and returns { complete, totalRequired, totalSatisfied, sections, missing } where missing is the list of applicable-but-unsatisfied rules (id, section, description) in rule order and sections is one bucket per section in first-appearance order (13 buckets when every section has an applicable rule). Conditional gating verified: Q1-02/03/04 apply only when the matching Q1 tick is true; Q2-02 vs Q2-03 by lastSeen; Q3-02 only on blackouts yes; Q4-02 on seizures yes; Q5-01 only on 'first-ever'; Q6a/Q6g/Q6i and the three Q6-EPI-* rules only on 'more-than-one-or-epilepsy' (Q6h additionally needs affectedConsciousness yes); Q7a-01 only when a named medication exists and noMedicationTaken is false; Q10a on double vision yes, Q10b-01 on suppressedOrControlled yes, Q10b-02 on correctionMethod 'other'; Q12a on needsAdaptations yes, Q12b on previouslyDeclared yes; AUTH-05/06 only when electronicCorrespondenceConsent is 'yes'. Flags are a SEPARATE export mirrored from form-app.js submitForm(): detectFlaggedIssues(state) with one argument, so flagsArgs is [\"state\"]; the oracle stores them as expected.flaggedIssues. Quirks verified: FLAG-SEIZ-003 tests only hadSeizures === 'yes' && multiple.twoOrMoreWithinFiveYears === 'yes' - it does NOT check diagnosis, so a stale 'yes' left over from the more-than-one branch still fires on a 'first-ever' form (FLAG-SEIZ-001/002 do check the diagnosis); FLAG-EPI-001 uses plain truthiness (!signedName) rather than hasText; the default medication.entries row { name: '', ... } is left in place when noMedicationTaken is ticked and is harmless because Q7-01/Q7a-01 use some(hasText(name)); flags are stable-sorted urgent > high > medium > low in push order. The grader result carries no timestamp (form-app.js adds one). Regenerate expected with: bin/test-personas united-kingdom-driver-and-vehicle-licensing-agency-b1-form --update",
